<!--
  MLIE_FAUNA_ABSORPTION_1 Wave C — Hawkbat creature port (Pass 12).
  Ported from mlie.starwarsanimalcollection's `Hawkbat` ThingDef/PawnKindDef
  pair (Races_Animal_SW.xml, workshop folder 3497316713), renamed under the
  RSW_ tier prefix. Geometry/stats/comps copied verbatim.

  Body: the donor's custom `Hawkbat` BodyDef needs its tail part repointed
  to the ALREADY-PORTED Wave B `RSW_SW_Club` BodyPartDef (the same club-tail
  Dragonsnake already reuses) plus its 2 wing parts repointed to the
  ALREADY-PORTED Wave B `RSW_SW_LeftWing`/`RSW_SW_RightWing` BodyPartDefs
  (the same pair CanCell/Bogwing already reuse) — every other part vanilla
  Core. Ported as RSW_Hawkbat (RSW_MlieWaveC_Bodies.xml).

  `leatherDef`/`specificMeatDef` repoint to the already-ported
  RSW_Leather_Reptavian/RSW_Reptavian_Meat (RSW_MlieWaveB_Resources.xml).
  Its 2 eggs are newly ported (RSW_EggHawkbatFertilized/UnFertilized,
  texPath swresource/EggPod — already extracted, Wave B/C, reused
  unchanged) with a new tasteThought (RSW_AteHawkbatEgg, added to
  RSW_Bantha_Thoughts.xml). No `canCrossBreedWith` in the donor.

  🔴 **ArtOverride collision avoided, checked BEFORE extracting anything**:
  `HawkbatArtOverride` (mandrake.rsw.hawkbatartoverride) exists and covers
  `Hawkbat_{east,north,south}` AND `Hawkbat_j_{east,north,south}` (the
  override's own About.xml explains it wires the SAME new art to both the
  base and female/juvenile facings, per the ART_REGEN_WAVE2_WIRE_IN_1
  alternate-variant precedent, so females don't silently keep the old donor
  look). The override does NOT touch the flying-animation frame set or the
  dessicated-corpse texture. Per the Dragonsnake/Anooba same-path-collision
  trap (2026-09-12 finding), SWBestiary ships ONLY `Hawkbat_Dessicated` plus
  all 24 flying-animation frames (`Hawkbat_Flying_1-4_{east,north,south}`
  and `Hawkbat_j_Flying_1-4_{east,north,south}`) — the 6 base/juvenile
  static facings are NOT extracted here, and the PawnKindDef's
  `bodyGraphicData`/`femaleGraphicData` texPaths below stay pointed at the
  donor's own `swanimals/Hawkbat/Hawkbat`/`Hawkbat_j` paths unmodified (same
  relative path HawkbatArtOverride uses, same load-order-wins mechanism as
  every other rename in this item).

  Art: 25 PNGs extracted this pass via extract_bundle.py against the live
  Steam workshop bundle (workshop folder 3497316713) — Hawkbat_Dessicated
  plus all 24 flying-animation frames, confirmed non-zero and PIL-openable.
  Sits at Textures/swanimals/Hawkbat/.

  Wired into the live cast this same pass: per cast_assignment.csv's own
  ground truth.
-->
<Defs>
<ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase" ADogSaidBody="LegsTail">
    <defName>RSW_Hawkbat</defName>
    <label>hawk-bat</label>
    <description>Hawk-bats were predatory reptavians with a curved beak and leathery wings that could be found on urbanized worlds like Coruscant and Taris. To get on a hawk-bat's bad side could be very dangerous. As a result, very few lived in captivity. Though they favored granite slugs, hawk-bats would feed on almost anything smaller than themselves. When they hatched from their eggs, young hawk-bats had scaly green skin and were precocial, meaning they were fully independent and able to hunt upon the day of hatching. Upon reaching maturity, the hawk-bat would shed its green skin and emerge with mature purplish-gray skin.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>3.5</MoveSpeed>
      <MarketValue>500</MarketValue>
      <ComfyTemperatureMin>0</ComfyTemperatureMin>
      <ComfyTemperatureMax>80</ComfyTemperatureMax>
      <ToxicResistance>1</ToxicResistance>
      <ToxicEnvironmentResistance MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">1.0</ToxicEnvironmentResistance>
      <Wildness>0.80</Wildness>
      <MaxFlightTime>120</MaxFlightTime>
      <FlightCooldown>10</FlightCooldown>
    </statBases>
    <tools>
      <li>
        <label>tail</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Scratch</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>7</power>
        <cooldownTime>2</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>RSW_SWTailAttackTool</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
        <surpriseAttack>
          <extraMeleeDamages>
            <li>
              <def>Stun</def>
              <amount>7</amount>
            </li>
          </extraMeleeDamages>
        </surpriseAttack>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>beak</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Bite</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>10</power>
        <cooldownTime>2</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>Beak</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
        <surpriseAttack>
          <extraMeleeDamages>
            <li>
              <def>Stun</def>
              <amount>6</amount>
            </li>
          </extraMeleeDamages>
        </surpriseAttack>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>head</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Blunt</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>4</power>
        <cooldownTime>1.5</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>HeadAttackTool</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
        <ensureLinkedBodyPartsGroupAlwaysUsable>true</ensureLinkedBodyPartsGroupAlwaysUsable>
        <chanceFactor>0.2</chanceFactor>
        <surpriseAttack>
          <extraMeleeDamages>
            <li>
              <def>Stun</def>
              <amount>6</amount>
            </li>
          </extraMeleeDamages>
        </surpriseAttack>
      </li>
    </tools>
    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties_EggLayer">
        <eggUnfertilizedDef>RSW_EggHawkbatUnFertilized</eggUnfertilizedDef>
        <eggFertilizedDef>RSW_EggHawkbatFertilized</eggFertilizedDef>
        <eggFertilizationCountMax>1</eggFertilizationCountMax>
        <eggLayIntervalDays>10</eggLayIntervalDays>
        <eggCountRange>1~2</eggCountRange>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <race>
      <body>RSW_Hawkbat</body>
      <predator>true</predator>
      <maxPreyBodySize>2.0</maxPreyBodySize>
      <baseHungerRate>0.75</baseHungerRate>
      <baseBodySize>2.0</baseBodySize>
      <baseHealthScale>0.50</baseHealthScale>
      <foodType>CarnivoreAnimal, OvivoreAnimal, AnimalProduct</foodType>
      <leatherDef>RSW_Leather_Reptavian</leatherDef>
